<title>USA: Ascent Entertainment Q1 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Ascent Entertainment Q1 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollar amounts in millions, except per share information)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							 Mar. 31,</p>
<p>						  1997		   1996</p>
<p> Revenues				     $89.9		 $72.3</p>
<p> Net loss				   ( 17.7)		( 4.3)</p>
<p> EBITDA					   1.9		  11.8</p>
<p> Net loss per common share	    ( 0.59)	     ( 0.14)</p>
<p> EBITDA per share			    0.06		  0.40</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>of common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding				 29.8		  29.8</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said its results reflected a satellite failure affecting SpectraVision rooms, lower revenues for the NBA Denver Nuggets and higher costs for the NHL Colorado Avalanche.</p>
<p>The full company name is Ascent Entertainment Group Inc.</p>
</text>
